~ # ping google.com // ipv4 works
PING google.com (142.250.195.238) 56(84) bytes of data.
64 bytes from maa03s43-in-f14.1e100.net (142.250.195.238): icmp_seq=1 ttl=112 time=62.0 ms
^C
--- google.com ping statistics ---
1 packets transmitted, 1 received, 0% packet loss, time 0ms
rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 62.039/62.039/62.039/0.000 ms

~ # ping6 google.com // ipv6 works
PING google.com(bom07s28-in-x0e.1e100.net) 56 data bytes
64 bytes from bom07s28-in-x0e.1e100.net: icmp_seq=1 ttl=117 time=78.1 ms
^C
--- google.com ping statistics ---
1 packets transmitted, 1 received, 0% packet loss, time 0ms
rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 78.133/78.133/78.133/0.000 ms

~ # ifconfig eth0 0 // Disabled ipv4... ipv6 still works...

~ # ping6 google.com // ip6 address resolution succeeds.
PING google.com(maa05s23-in-x0e.1e100.net) 56 data bytes
64 bytes from maa05s23-in-x0e.1e100.net: icmp_seq=1 ttl=116 time=68.3 ms
^C
--- google.com ping statistics ---
1 packets transmitted, 1 received, 0% packet loss, time 0ms
rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 68.319/68.319/68.319/0.000 ms

~ # ping google.com  // ipv4 address resolution fails..
connect: Network is unreachable

~ # ifconfig eth0 down // reconfigure the eth0 network..


~ # ping google.com // ipv4 works
PING google.com (142.250.195.238) 56(84) bytes of data.
64 bytes from maa03s43-in-f14.1e100.net (142.250.195.238): icmp_seq=2 ttl=112 time=69.8 ms
64 bytes from maa03s43-in-f14.1e100.net (142.250.195.238): icmp_seq=3 ttl=112 time=67.1 ms
^C
--- google.com ping statistics ---
3 packets transmitted, 2 received, 33% packet loss, time 2002ms
rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 67.172/68.532/69.892/1.360 ms

~ # ping6 google.com // ipv6 works
PING google.com(maa03s43-in-x0e.1e100.net) 56 data bytes
64 bytes from maa03s43-in-x0e.1e100.net: icmp_seq=1 ttl=117 time=85.0 ms
^C
--- google.com ping statistics ---
1 packets transmitted, 1 received, 0% packet loss, time 0ms
rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 85.058/85.058/85.058/0.000 ms



